  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\n\nAs the H5 wave ejects east, should see sfc high pressure centered \nover most of Ontario extend westward toward the Northern Plains. As \na result, expect primarily dry conditions Tuesday and most of \nWednesday. By late Wednesday into Thursday, should see warm \nadvection return along with a mid-level impulse. This will \nresult in our next best chance at some rain, with PoPs of 50 to \n70% across our western areas. We'll return into a southwesterly \nflow regime for the rest of the extended period resulting in \ncontinued 20-30% chances for rain. Temperatures remain cool in \nthe 60s for Tuesday through Friday before warming to the 70s by \nnext Saturday.",
